<h1>🏦 BankingApp — Codebase Architecture & Environment Guide</h1>
<p>This document provides a complete reference for the Global Banking Application codebase: its architecture, multi-environment CI/CD strategy, infrastructure provisioning, Kubernetes deployments, and developer workflows.</p>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<h2>1. High-Level Architecture</h2>

<div class="flow-diagram">
  <div class="flow-box">Developer<br>Push</div>
  <div class="flow-arrow">→</div>
  <div class="flow-box">GitHub<br>Branch</div>
  <div class="flow-arrow">→</div>
  <div class="flow-box">GitHub<br>Actions</div>
  <div class="flow-arrow">→</div>
  <div class="flow-box">Docker<br>Build + ECR</div>
  <div class="flow-arrow">→</div>
  <div class="flow-box">Helm<br>Deploy</div>
  <div class="flow-arrow">→</div>
  <div class="flow-box">EKS<br>Namespace</div>
</div>

<p>The application runs on a <strong>shared AWS EKS cluster</strong> with three Kubernetes namespaces providing environment isolation:</p>

<table>
<tr><th>Branch</th><th>Environment</th><th>K8s Namespace</th><th>Approval?</th></tr>
<tr><td><code>dev</code></td><td>Development</td><td><code>banking-dev</code></td><td><span class="badge badge-green">No</span></td></tr>
<tr><td><code>test</code></td><td>Test / QA</td><td><code>banking-test</code></td><td><span class="badge badge-green">No</span></td></tr>
<tr><td><code>prod</code></td><td>Production</td><td><code>banking-prod</code></td><td><span class="badge badge-red">Yes — Required</span></td></tr>
</table>

<div class="note">
  <strong>Key Design Decision:</strong> A single EKS cluster with namespace-based isolation (instead of 3 separate clusters) keeps AWS costs low while providing full environment separation via Kubernetes RBAC, resource quotas, and network policies.
</div>

