<h2>5. CI/CD Workflows</h2>

<h3>5.1 <code>apply.yml</code> — Application Deployment</h3>

<div class="flow-diagram">
  <div class="flow-box">Push to<br>dev/test/prod</div>
  <div class="flow-arrow">→</div>
  <div class="flow-box">Set<br>Environment</div>
  <div class="flow-arrow">→</div>
  <div class="flow-box">Build &<br>Push Images</div>
  <div class="flow-arrow">→</div>
  <div class="flow-box">Helm<br>Deploy</div>
  <div class="flow-arrow">→</div>
  <div class="flow-box">Sync to<br>EC2</div>
</div>

<table>
<tr><th>Step</th><th>Job</th><th>Description</th></tr>
<tr><td>1</td><td><code>set-environment</code></td><td>Detects environment from branch name (e.g., push to <code>prod</code> → env=prod)</td></tr>
<tr><td>2</td><td><code>build-images</code></td><td>Builds 5 Docker images, pushes to ECR with both <code>sha</code> and <code>latest</code> tags</td></tr>
<tr><td>3</td><td><code>deploy-helm</code></td><td>Runs <code>helm upgrade --install</code> with base + environment-specific values</td></tr>
<tr><td>4</td><td><code>sync-ec2</code></td><td>rsyncs the repo to the EC2 Nginx instance for reference</td></tr>
</table>

<div class="warn">
  <strong>Production Approval:</strong> The <code>build-images</code> and <code>deploy-helm</code> jobs both specify <code>environment: ${{ needs.set-environment.outputs.environment }}</code>. When this resolves to <code>prod</code>, GitHub requires reviewer approval before the job runs. This is configured in <strong>GitHub → Settings → Environments → prod → Required reviewers</strong>.
</div>

<h3>5.2 <code>infra.yml</code> — Infrastructure Management</h3>
<p>Manual-only workflow (<code>workflow_dispatch</code>). Runs Terraform init/plan/apply for the shared EKS cluster. Also runs Ansible to configure the EC2 Nginx instance.</p>

<h3>5.3 <code>destroy.yml</code> — Teardown</h3>
<p>Manual workflow with two options:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>App only</strong> (default): Uninstalls Helm release + deletes namespace for the selected environment</li>
  <li><strong>App + Infra</strong> (<code>destroy_infra=true</code>): Also runs <code>terraform destroy</code> to remove the entire cluster (requires <code>prod</code> environment approval)</li>
</ul>

