<h2>8. Production Approval Setup</h2>

<p>The approval mechanism uses <strong>GitHub Environments</strong> — no custom code needed.</p>

<h3>Step-by-Step Configuration</h3>
<ol>
  <li>Navigate to your repository on GitHub</li>
  <li>Go to <strong>Settings → Environments</strong></li>
  <li>Click <strong>New environment</strong> and create:
    <ul>
      <li><code>dev</code> — no protection rules</li>
      <li><code>test</code> — no protection rules</li>
      <li><code>prod</code> — enable <strong>Required reviewers</strong> and add your team</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
  <li>Optionally add <strong>Deployment branches</strong> rule to <code>prod</code> to restrict to the <code>prod</code> branch only</li>
</ol>

<div class="note">
  When a developer pushes to the <code>prod</code> branch, the workflow starts but the <code>build-images</code> job enters a "Waiting" state. Designated reviewers receive a notification and must click <strong>"Approve and run"</strong> before any build or deployment happens. Dev and test branches deploy automatically with no approval.
</div>

