<h2>11. Kubernetes In-Cluster Request Flow</h2>

<div class="flow-diagram">
  <div class="flow-box">User<br>Browser</div>
  <div class="flow-arrow">→</div>
  <div class="flow-box">AWS ALB<br>(Ingress)</div>
  <div class="flow-arrow">→</div>
  <div class="flow-box">ingress-nginx<br>Controller</div>
  <div class="flow-arrow">→</div>
  <div class="flow-box">Frontend<br>(Nginx :80)</div>
  <div class="flow-arrow">→</div>
  <div class="flow-box">Backend<br>Services</div>
</div>

<p>Within the cluster:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Frontend</strong> calls <strong>User Service</strong> (:8000) and <strong>Transaction Service</strong> (:8080)</li>
  <li><strong>Transaction Service</strong> publishes events to <strong>Kafka</strong> (:29092)</li>
  <li><strong>Activity Service</strong> (:8001) consumes from Kafka</li>
  <li>Services cache sessions in <strong>Redis</strong> (:6379)</li>
  <li>All services read/write from <strong>PostgreSQL</strong> (:5432)</li>
</ul>

